@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+---
+sidebar_label: Request scheduling intent
+---
+
+# Opt-in request scheduling intent
+
+For a custom Strata endpoint that supports `strata_scheduling`, a host can enable
+automatic self-demotion in its provider configuration:
+
+```yaml
+providers:
+  strata:
+    api: http://127.0.0.1:18097/v1
+    default_model: your-local-model
+    transport: chat_completions
+    request_scheduling:
+      enabled: true
+```
+
+The legacy `custom_providers` entry accepts the same field. The setting is absent
+and off by default; only an exact boolean `enabled`, with no additional policy
+keys, is accepted. It does not enable Strata's server-side queue. Provider name,
+resolved endpoint and model/catalog must match the configured entry. An ambiguous
+bare `custom` route with conflicting entries stays off. Configuration is read in
+the active profile on each request, without a separate global policy cache.
+
+Hermes derives intent from host facts, never from message text:
+
+| Origin | Automatic request class |
+| --- | --- |
+| User conversation, including tool-loop continuations | Default normal |
+| Host-created subagent or cron agent | Background |
+| Exact `background_review` turn origin | Background |
+| `/btw`, unknown fork origin, or parent session ID alone | Default normal |
+| Auxiliary call with a nonempty task identifier | Background |
+| Auxiliary call without a task identifier | Default normal |
+
+This initial opt-in also demotes foreground-dependent auxiliary tasks such as
+vision and compression. Enable it only when that policy fits the endpoint's
+queue. Classification neither authorizes a request nor reserves capacity, changes
+model quality, preempts running work, or bypasses a resource lease.
+
+The existing SDK serializes `extra_body.strata_scheduling` as the top-level
+`strata_scheduling: {class: background}` field. Generation is local to each
+assembled request; it never modifies parent overrides, shared config, prompts,
+or fallback source data. The fallback assembler checks the resolved destination
+again. A manually supplied background remains background. An explicit normal
+can self-demote under the opt-in; malformed existing scheduling metadata on a
+request being demoted raises `ValueError` before dispatch. Normal/off paths leave
+manual settings untouched, subject to the server's own validation.
+
+The integration is qualified here on Chat Completions using the real main and
+public sync/async auxiliary builders and actual SDK HTTP serialization. Other
+wire adapters and live priority improvement require their own acceptance tests.
